# The `build` tool (caos SPEC, "Tools"): this directory's worker script curried
# onto the Nim worker image, plus the `help` an agent registers it by.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so they live here rather than in the script's
# header — and a `.caos-expr` is STRIPPED from the tree its own expression is
# evaluated against, so editing them re-keys this tool's arg tree and NOTHING
# it builds. Rewording `@param [build-salt]` costs one arg-tree key; it does not
# recompile a line of Nim.
HELP=<<END
Compile the game server (src/ctf.nim) inside caos and return its diagnostics.
The Nim deps come from a cached `deps` job keyed on nimby.lock, and the C
compilation is ccache-backed, so an unchanged build never runs and a one-file
edit recompiles one file. Nothing is handed in from the host: the tree is
compiled from source, in workers.
@param [build-salt] Force a rebuild — any fresh value (e.g. $(date --iso=s)) re-keys this build and nothing else.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/nim --worker1:@=worker.sh --help=$HELP
